.DS_Store
/tests
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# MEX sources and anything used to build them. The compiled binaries are what
# ships -- the .mex files for each platform, and libfftw3-3.dll beside ringRm --
# so the sources the vendors compile them from stay out of the repository.
#
# There are no MEX project or makefile artefacts in the tree; the rules for them
# are here so that adding one does not quietly commit it.
*.c
*.cpp
*.cc
*.cxx
*.cu
*.cuh
*.h
*.hpp
*.vcxproj
*.vcxproj.*
*.sln
Makefile
makefile
*.mk

# Build folders, excluded whole rather than by extension, so that anything else
# put in them is covered too. What the app needs at run time sits outside them
# and stays committed: the four ringRm.mex files and libfftw3-3.dll, and the
# eight NLMF denoising mex files.
functions/unRing/OSX/
functions/unRing/Windows/
functions/denoise/NLMFdenoise/source/
retrospective10.mlapp.bak
STATUS.md

# The manuals themselves are committed. Only the Pages source of the app manual
# is not: it is the 13 MB editable original, and the PDF exported from it beside
# it is the one people read.
manuals/*.pages

# Files that ship as .p
#
# The rule: where a .p exists beside a .m, the .p is what is committed and the
# .m stays local. Regenerate this list after p-coding a new source, or after
# moving one -- an entry naming a file that has moved silently stops ignoring
# anything, and the source gets committed.
